        costEffect: "**Partly passed on.** It raised consumer prices 3–10% in Q4 FY26 and again in April and May, covering 6–13% cost inflation with price rises and savings; gross margin rose 1.3 points in Q1 FY27. Fixed-price professional lighting contracts signed before the war could not be repriced. **Rule of thumb:** a 10% rise in material costs not passed on would cut the margin by about 7 points (3% to about −4%, a loss). **What happened:** India's copper price index rose from 100 in Q1 FY24 to 149 in Q1 FY27, while the margin went from 6.1% to 7.1%. Copper was not the main driver: the margin collapsed to 0.8% in Q3 FY26 as it cleared old stock and lost fan share, then recovered on cost cuts and price rises. The company's own Q1 FY27 segment profit also included ₹26cr of other income.",
